| `evals.live.model_options.<name>` | any | `{}` | keyword arguments the adapter `evals.live.model` names accepts, such as `base_url` and `model` for `openai-compatible` | `evals/_run.py` (`run_live`, through `models.get_model`) | Passed to the adapter's constructor; an argument it does not accept, or accepts and refuses (for `openai-compatible`, an `api_key_env` that `models.credential_env.openai-compatible` does not declare, a `base_url` that is not an http or https URL with a host and no user part, query or fragment, an http `base_url` whose host is not a loopback address literal, or a `base_url` whose host and port `models.allowed_hosts.openai-compatible` does not list), is refused with exit 2 before any call. | a credential: `models.credential_env` | always |
